  "notes": "Multi-instrumentalist rock-into-pop producer bridging legacy rock acts and chart pop. The drums are the hardest-hitting in this batch and the research says so: \"plays drums himself; a hard, dry, compressed rock backbeat with crash accents on chorus downbeats and minimal hat detail.\" So the snare is `hard` transient under a `short` tail with the highest velocity tiers in this batch, `hihat.fillDensity` falls to 0.14 with no roll vocabulary, and `crash` leads the perc lanes at `downbeat` placement. \"His method is putting seasoned rock players and pop artists in the same room\" is the played humanize block. No `bass808` block: \"no 808 in the rock mode — he plays bass guitar, doubling the guitar's root rhythm; the pop-facing records add a synth sub under it\", which is `mirror_kick` at a high `followRootsProb` with root-fifth cells — doubling the guitar root, not walking. Harmony is \"guitar-idiomatic keys (E, A, D, G) with blues-scale melodic borrowing on the rock records and diatonic pop harmony on the pop records\", so the key list is his and `major_blues` carries weight alongside major. \"Loops are 4 or 8 bars with a real chorus lift\" is the cadential family set, and \"countermelody is a guitar line\" is `answer_lick` first. The arrangement is the giveaway and is authored literally: \"verse—chorus—solo—chorus rock form even on pop records\", which is why the higher-weighted structure carries a bridge slot used as a solo and the fills land every four bars. ⚠ `confidence` is medium against a medium-high rating because the research says \"key and harmonic specifics inferred\": every drum probability, the humanize numbers, the harmonic weights and `bpm.mode` 115 (the midpoint of the stated 80—150 band) are INFERRED, and the entry's [LOW-CONF] mark on the key/blues claim is repeated here.",
